<title>USA: Warner Bros. signs Pay TV deal in Spain.</title>
<headline>Warner Bros. signs Pay TV deal in Spain.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Time Warner Inc's Warner Bros. International Television said Wednesday it concluded a far-reaching pay television deal with Sogecable in Spain.</p>
<p>Under terms of the deal, Warner Bros. will provide Sogecable's Canal Satelite Digital and its premium pay television service Canal Plus Spain with pay television, pay-per-view and near video on demand feature films.</p>
<p>The agreement also calls for carriage of three cable channels from Turner Broadcasting International, including the Cartoon Network, TNT, and CNN International.</p>
<p>Financial terms of the agreement were not disclosed.</p>
